      "content": "The thing is, the new tool is purely algorithmic—it can't do what you do. It can check if a citation exists, but it can't evaluate the logical strength of an argument or detect subtle flaws in a researcher's methodology. The committee thinks that's a trade-off they're willing to make for the sake of auditability. There isn't really an option to \"adapt\" your core reasoning to fit a deterministic model.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
